Agenda
THE CORPORATION OF THE
TOWN OF GEORGINA
Committee of Adjustment
Monday, September 28, 2026
7:30 PM
1.
ROLL CALL
 “The Town of Georgina recognizes and acknowledges that we are on lands originally used and occupied by the First Peoples of the Williams Treaties First Nations and other Indigenous Peoples, and on behalf of the Mayor and Council, we would like to thank them for sharing this land.  We would also like to acknowledge the Chippewas of Georgina Island First Nation as our close neighbour and friend, one with which we strive to build a cooperative and respectful relationship.

We also recognize the unique relationship the Chippewas have with the lands and waters of this territory.  They are the water protectors and environmental stewards of these lands and we join them in these responsibilities.”
2.
INTRODUCTION OF ADDENDUM ITEM(S)
 3.
DECLARATION OF PECUNIARY INTEREST
 4.
EXPLANATION OF HEARING PROCEDURE
 5.
REQUESTS FOR DEFERRAL OR WITHDRAWAL
 6.
APPLICATIONS FOR CONSENT
 1.
CONSENT APPLICATION CON-2026-0013, CON-2026-0014 810 AND 812 ROCKAWAY ROAD LOTS 5 AND 6, AND PART LOT 7, PL
  That the Committee of Adjustment approve Consent Application CON-2026-0013 as it pertains to the property municipally addressed as 810 and 812 Rockaway Road to sever and convey the Subject Land “B” from the Retained Land “C”, as shown in Attachment 2 to Report No. DS-2026-0061, to create one (1) new residential building lot; and,
That the approval of Consent Application CON-2026-0013 be subject to the following conditions:
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of two (2) white prints of a deposited reference plan of survey to conform substantially with the applications, as submitted;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of a draft deed, in duplicate, conveying Subject Land ‘B’ from Retained Land ‘C’ as shown on Attachment 2 to Report No. DS-2026-0053;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of written confirmation from the Town of Georgina Development Planning Division that all structures have been removed from the subject and retained land, to the satisfaction of the Development Planning Division;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of written confirmation from the Town of Georgina Policy Planning Division that an Arborist Report and Tree Preservation Plan has been provided, to the satisfaction of the Policy Planning Division;
That Section 50(5) of the Planning Act shall apply to any future conveyance of the Subject Land “B”, as shown on Attachment 2;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of written confirmation from The Town of Georgina Development Engineering Division that all Engineering matters identified in Attachment 4 have been addressed to the Division’s satisfaction;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of written confirmation from York Region that all matters identified in Attachment 4 have been addressed to the Region’s satisfaction;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of written confirmation from the Town of Georgina Development Planning Division that a municipal address has been tentatively assigned to the Subject Land;
That the above-noted condition(s) be fulfilled within two (2) years of the date of the Notice of Decision.
3. That the Committee of Adjustment approve Consent Application CON-2026-0014 as it pertains to the property municipally addressed as 810 and 812 Rockaway Road to sever and convey the Subject Land “A” from the Retained Land “B”, as shown in Attachment 2 to Report No. DS-2026-0061, to create one (1) new residential building lot; and,
4. That the approval of Consent Application CON-2026-00014 be subject to the following conditions:
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of two (2) white prints of a deposited reference plan of survey to conform substantially with the applications, as submitted;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of a draft deed, in duplicate, conveying Subject Land ‘A’ from Retained Land ‘B’ as shown on Attachment 2 to Report No. DS-2026-0053;
That the Committee Reserve 2.8 persons equivalent of Sanitary Sewer and Water Allocation for the proposed development from Category 5- Willow Beach / Serviced Lakeshore Residential for a period of up to 2 years, and that the ‘Reserved’ servicing allocation be formally ‘Committed’ and assigned by the Director of Development Services upon the issuance of the Certificate of Official;
That the ‘Reserved’ servicing allocation be automatically rescinded in the event that conditions of provisional consent are not fulfilled prior to the two-year lapsing date as specified in the Notice of Decision;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of confirmation that Consent Application CON-2026-0013 is approved and that all conditions of approval associated with CON-2026-0013 have been fulfilled to the satisfaction of the Town;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of written confirmation from the Town of Georgina Development Planning Division that all structures have been removed from the subject and retained land, to the satisfaction of the Development Planning Division;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of written confirmation from the Town of Georgina Policy Planning Division that an Arborist Report and Tree Preservation Plan has been provided, to the satisfaction of the Policy Planning Division;
That Section 50(5) of the Planning Act shall apply to any future conveyance of the Subject Land “A”, as shown on Attachment 2;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of written confirmation from The Town of Georgina Development Engineering Division that all Engineering matters identified in Attachment 4 have been addressed to the Division’s satisfaction;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of written confirmation from York Region that all matters identified in Attachment 4 have been addressed to the Region’s satisfaction;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of written confirmation from the Town of Georgina Development Planning Division that a municipal address has been tentatively assigned to the Subject Land;
That the above-noted condition(s) be fulfilled within two (2) years of the date of the Notice of Decision.
2.
CONSENT APPLICATIONS CON-2026-0017, CON-2026-0018,
  That the Committee of Adjustment approve Consent Application CON-2026-0017, as it pertains to the subject lands, to convey a drainage easement over Subject Lands ‘A’ in favour of Beneficiary Lands ‘C’, as shown in Attachment 3 to Report No. DS-2026-0062;
That the approval of Consent Application CON-2026-0017 be subject to the following conditions:
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of two (2) white prints of a deposited reference plan of survey to conform substantially with the application, as submitted;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of draft transfer documents, in duplicate, conveying Subject Lands ‘A’ to Beneficiary Lands ‘C’, as shown in Attachment 3 to Report No. DS-2026-0062;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of confirmation that Consent Application CON-2026-0020 is approved and that all conditions of approval associated with Consent Application CON-2026-0020 have been fulfilled to the satisfaction of the Town;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of written confirmation from the Town of Georgina Development Engineering Division that a Stormwater Management Brief and Drawing, as well as a Lot Grading and Drainage Plan, have been provided to the satisfaction of the Development Engineering Division; and,
That the above-noted conditions be fulfilled within two (2) years of the date of the Notice of Decision.
3. That the Committee of Adjustment approve Consent Application CON-2026-0018, as it pertains to the subject lands, to convey a drainage easement over Subject Lands ‘A’ in favour of Beneficiary Lands ‘B’ and Beneficiary Lands ‘C’, as shown in Attachment 3 to Report No. DS-2026-0062;
4. That the approval of Consent Application CON-2026-0018 be subject to the following conditions:
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of two (2) white prints of a deposited reference plan of survey to conform substantially with the application, as submitted;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of draft transfer documents, in duplicate, conveying Subject Lands ‘A’ to Beneficiary Lands ‘B’ and Beneficiary Lands ‘C’, as shown in Attachment 3 to Report No. DS-2026-0062;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of confirmation that Consent Application CON-2026-0020 is approved and that all conditions of approval associated with Consent Application CON-2026-0020 have been fulfilled to the satisfaction of the Town;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of written confirmation from the Town of Georgina Development Engineering Division that a Stormwater Management Brief and Drawing, as well as a Lot Grading and Drainage Plan, have been provided to the satisfaction of the Development Engineering Division; and,
That the above-noted conditions be fulfilled within two (2) years of the date of the Notice of Decision.
5. That the Committee of Adjustment approve Consent Application CON-2026-0019, as it pertains to the subject lands, to convey a drainage easement over Subject Lands ‘A’ in favour of Beneficiary Lands ‘B’ and Beneficiary Lands ‘C’, as shown in Attachment 3 to Report No. DS-2026-0062;
6. That the approval of Consent Application CON-2026-0019 be subject to the following conditions:
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of two (2) white prints of a deposited reference plan of survey to conform substantially with the application, as submitted;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of draft transfer documents, in duplicate, conveying Subject Lands ‘A’ to Beneficiary Lands ‘B’ and Beneficiary Lands ‘C’, as shown in Attachment 3 to Report No. DS-2026-0062;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of confirmation that Consent Application CON-2026-0020 is approved and that all conditions of approval associated with Consent Application CON-2026-0020 have been fulfilled to the satisfaction of the Town;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of written confirmation from the Town of Georgina Development Engineering Division that a Stormwater Management Brief and Drawing, as well as a Lot Grading and Drainage Plan, have been provided to the satisfaction of the Development Engineering Division; and,
That the above-noted conditions be fulfilled within two (2) years of the date of the Notice of Decision.
7. That the Committee of Adjustment approve Consent Application No. CON-2026-0020, as it pertains to the subject lands, to sever and convey Subject Lands ‘A’ from Remainder Lands ‘B’ and add it to Beneficiary Lands ‘C’, as shown in Attachment 4 to Report No. DS-2026-0062;
8. That the approval of Consent Application CON-2026-0020 be subject to the following conditions:
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of two (2) white prints of a deposited reference plan of survey to conform substantially with the application, as submitted;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of draft transfer documents, in duplicate, conveying Subject Lands ‘A’ to Beneficiary Lands ‘C’, as indicated in Attachment 4 to Report No. DS-2026-0062;
That Sections 50(3) and 50(5) of the Planning Act shall apply to any subsequent conveyance of, or transaction involving the Subject Land “A”, as shown on Attachment 4; and
That the above-noted conditions be fulfilled within two (2) years of the date of the Notice of Decision.
3.
CONSENT APPLICATIONS CON-2025-0014, CON-2025-0015, CON-2025-0016 CHURCH STREET AND 213 SHORECREST ROAD
  That the Committee of Adjustment approve Consent Application CON-2025-0014 as they pertain to the property municipally addressed as Church Street to sever and convey an approximate 3 metre driveway easement over Servient Land ‘A’ in favour of the neighbouring property to the North (Benefiting Land ‘A’) for access, as shown in Attachment 2 to Report No. DS-2026-0053; and,
That the approval of Consent Application CON-2025-0014 be subject to the following conditions:
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of two (2) white prints of a deposited reference plan of survey to conform substantially with the application, as submitted;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of a draft deed, in duplicate, conveying an easement over Servient Land ‘A’ in favour of Benefiting Lands ‘A’ to the north, as shown on Attachment 2 to Report No. DS-2026-0053;
That the above-noted condition(s) be fulfilled within two (2) years of the date of the Notice of Decision;
3. That the Committee of Adjustment approve Consent Application CON-2025-0015 as they pertain to the property municipally addressed as 213 Shorecrest Road to convey an approximate 3 metre driveway easement over Servient Land ‘B’ in favour of the neighbouring property to the North (Benefiting Land ‘A’) for access, as shown in Attachment 2 to Report No. DS-2026-0053; and,
4. That the approval of Consent Application CON-2025-0015 be subject to the following conditions:
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of two (2) white prints of a deposited reference plan of survey to conform substantially with the application, as submitted;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of a draft deed, in duplicate, conveying an easement over Servient Land ‘B’ in favour of Benefiting Land ‘A’ to the north, as shown on Attachment 2 to Report No. DS-2026-0053;
That the above-noted condition(s) be fulfilled within two (2) years of the date of the Notice of Decision.
4. That the Committee of Adjustment approve Consent Application CON-2025-0016 as they pertain to the property municipally addressed as 213 Shorecrest Road to sever and convey Severed Land from Retained Land, and convey the same to the Benefiting Land ‘B’ as shown in Attachment 2 to Report No. DS-2026-0053; and
5. That the approval of Consent Application CON-2025-0016 be subject to the following conditions:
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of two (2) white prints of a deposited reference plan of survey to conform substantially with the applications, as submitted;
Submission to the Secretary-Treasurer of a draft transfer, in duplicate, conveying Severed Land to Benefiting Land ‘B’ as shown on Attachment 2 to Report No. DS-2026-0053;
That Section 50(5) of the Planning Act shall apply to any future conveyance of the Severed Land, as shown on Attachment 2;
That the above-noted condition(s) be fulfilled within two (2) years of the date of the Notice of Decision.
  7.
APPLICATIONS FOR MINOR VARIANCE
 8.
POWER OF SALE/FORECLOSURE/VALIDATION OF TITLE APPLICATIONS
 9.
MINUTES OF PREVIOUS MEETING
 10.
COMMUNICATIONS
 11.
OTHER BUSINESS
 12.
NEXT MEETING
 October 19, 2026
13.
ADJOURNMENT
